|~ `::group`, the steps in parentheses run on the value in the pipe, and
   what is declared under it: its constructor and its refusals.
   The decisions it exists for: [D114]. ~|

:group
  |~~ A group, `(…)`, runs a pipeline as one word: its steps run on the
      value in the pipe, it answers what its last step answers, and the
      names it declares stay inside. Each part of a literal is one,
      which is why a literal is the shape an answer takes,
      `5 | get [(add 1) (mul 2)]` answering `[6 10]`, and a modifier of more
      than one word stands in one, `take (count | sub 1)`.

      In a quote the step is a record that wraps the quote of its
      pipeline, `~((add 1 | mul 2)) | first` answering
      `::group~(add 1 | mul 2)`.
      ::link~(::bind | doc) ::link~(::qlang/pipeline | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps
        |~~ The quote of a pipeline, built into the step `(pipeline)`. ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotQuoteError
        |~~ The payload of `::group` is the quote of its pipeline, so
            `~(add 1 | mul 2) | tag ::group` is the step
            `(add 1 | mul 2)`.
            ::link~(::group | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :ReadBackDiffersError
        |~~ The `::group` prints as text that reads back as another step,
            or as none, and `:printed` is that text: an empty group prints
            as `()`, which reads as no step. A group holds one step at
            least, and `it` keeps the value as it is,
            `~(it) | tag ::group`.
            ::link~(::group | doc)
        ~~|
    | proves :holdsItsSteps
        |~~ A group holds its steps. ~~|
        ~(~((add 1 | mul 2)) | first | payload | count | eq 2)
    | proves :PayloadNotQuoteError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(42 | tag ::group !| [type (get /actualType)] | eq [::group/PayloadNotQuoteError ::number])
    | proves :PayloadNotQuoteError/buildsTheStepOfAPipeline
        |~~ The quote of a pipeline builds the group that runs it. ~~|
        ~(~(add 1 | mul 2) | tag ::group | get [it] | tag ::quote | eq ~((add 1 | mul 2)))
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAnEmptyGroup
        |~~ An empty group prints as text that reads back as none. ~~|
        ~(~() | tag ::group !| [type (get /printed)] | eq [::group/ReadBackDiffersError "()"])
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/keepsTheValueByTheWholeValue
        |~~ A group of `it` is a step that keeps the value. ~~|
        ~(~(it) | tag ::group | get [it] | tag ::quote | eq ~((it)))
    | impl ::builtin{}

